1
00:03:27,692 --> 00:03:33,692
The stars that burn brightest burn quickest

2
00:06:55,384 --> 00:07:01,384
James Dean is a drama, tv movie film directed by Mark Rydell.

3
00:10:23,076 --> 00:10:29,076
The man behind the legend and a knowing look at 1950s Hollywood are revealed in this dynamic biopic of the meteoric star
whose troubled life echoed his gut-grabbing performances in East of Eden, Rebel Without a Cause and Giant.

4
00:13:50,769 --> 00:13:56,769
James Dean, played by James Franco.

5
00:17:18,461 --> 00:17:24,461
Winton Dean, played by Michael Moriarty.

6
00:20:46,153 --> 00:20:52,153
Pier Angeli, played by Valentina Cervi.

7
00:24:13,846 --> 00:24:19,846
Elia Kazan, played by Enrico Colantoni.

8
00:27:41,538 --> 00:27:47,538
Raymond Massey, played by Edward Herrmann.

9
00:31:09,230 --> 00:31:15,230
Hedda Hopper, played by Joanne Linville.

10
00:34:36,923 --> 00:34:42,923
James Dean is a 2001 American made-for-television biographical drama
film based on the life of the American actor James Dean.

11
00:38:04,615 --> 00:38:10,615
James Franco plays the title role under the direction of Mark Rydell, who chronicles Dean's
rise from a struggling actor to an A-list movie star in 1950s Hollywood.

12
00:41:32,307 --> 00:41:38,307
The film's supporting roles included Michael Moriarty, Valentina
Cervi, Enrico Colantoni, and Edward Herrmann.

13
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The biopic began development at Warner Bros.

14
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
in the early 1990s.

15
00:51:55,384 --> 00:52:01,384
At one point, Michael Mann was contracted to direct with
Leonardo DiCaprio starring in the lead role.

16
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
After Mann's departure, Des McAnuff, Dennis Hopper, and Milčo
Mančevski were considered for the director's chair.

17
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Rydell was hired as director in 1996, but the film
continued to languish in development hell.

18
01:02:18,461 --> 01:02:24,461
Warner Bros.

19
01:05:46,153 --> 01:05:52,153
then decided to produce James Dean as a TV movie for Turner
Network Television (TNT); both Warner Bros.

20
01:09:13,846 --> 01:09:19,846
and TNT were owned by Time Warner.

21
01:12:41,538 --> 01:12:47,538
Franco was cast as Dean in May 2000 after a search
that resulted in 500 auditions.

22
01:16:09,230 --> 01:16:15,230
Franco researched his role to closely portray Dean.

23
01:19:36,923 --> 01:19:42,923
James Dean was shown on TNT in the United States on August 5, 2001, receiving generally
positive reviews from critics and widespread acclaim for Franco's performance.

24
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:10,615
The film explores themes of musician, icon, biography, hollywood, dying young.

25
01:26:32,307 --> 01:26:38,307
The tone is emotional.
